WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:46.000
It's your last chance.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Hot.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Hoot.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Shoot.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Shot.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Chief has a one-track mind.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Lost.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Chief Ironside's office.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Yeah, she's right here.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.000
Yes?

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Yes, I have.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
When?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.000
I'll be right there.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
Anything wrong?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.000
I'll tell you about it in the morning.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:29.000
♪

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Oh, my dear.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Kim?

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Honey, what happened?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.000
I just ran a stoplight.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Honey, you wouldn't be here for that.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.000
John?

00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.000
Have a seat, Eve.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Cut the formalities, John. What happened?

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Driving under the influence.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Drinking?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Kim?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.000
You didn't let me finish.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Driving under the influence of and in possession of marijuana...

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.000
and dangerous drugs.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000
♪

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Why, Kim? Why?

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.000
I told you I didn't do anything.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.000
I just ran a red light.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Where did the drugs come from?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.000
I don't know.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.000
Really, a cop just looked in my purse, and there they were.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Do her parents know she's here?

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
They're not home.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:56.000
If you lie to me, I can't help you.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Oh, I'm not lying.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.000
Where were you tonight?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.000
I was at a party.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Maybe that's it.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Maybe somebody put them in my purse by mistake.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.000
Where was the party?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.000
Was it a friend's?

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.000
What friend?

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.000
What are you trying to do?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.000
Help you.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Well, don't give me the third degree.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.000
Can I take her home?

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.000
Ooh.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.000
Well, she'll have to be back here at 10 with her parents.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.000
All right.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.000
If I can reach them, I'll tell them you're on the way.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:31.000
Thank you.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Honey, am I really in trouble?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Yes.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:41.000
But if you're lucky, the worst you'll get will be probation.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.000
I doubt that.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.000
Why?

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:53.000
She's already on probation.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.000
The candy cane slips from your hand.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.000
Magician draws the curtain.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.000
The crutch you held to help you stand

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.000
Has made you feel uncertain.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.000
You walked across a river bridge

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.000
One day when you were smiling

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Now the sun has turned to brick

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.000
The road you're on is winding

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:23.000
You lost your way the other day

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:29.000
Seeking the melody man

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.000
La la la.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:39.000
La la la la la la la la la la la.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.980
La la la.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.480
La la la.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:48.960
La la la la la la.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.940
La la la la la la.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.900
Remind me to have Amy fill that.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:07.900
Oh, baby.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:09.900
Will you take it easy?

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:13.900
Let's not lose our heads when we get here, huh?

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:14.900
All right?

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:16.900
No, of course not.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:19.900
This is only the second time my daughter's been picked up with drugs.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.900
There's no reason to lose our heads, is there?

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:39.900
Getting angry won't help.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:40.900
Daddy.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:41.900
Hi.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:42.900
Thanks, Eve.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.900
I'm sorry to put you to so much trouble.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.900
That's the least of the trouble.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:49.900
Oh, Kim, my poor baby.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.900
I've been so worried about you.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:52.900
Don't worry.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:54.900
Everything's going to be all right.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:55.900
Carolyn, please.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:56.900
Please.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:58.900
Ted, what are we going to do?

00:05:58.900 --> 00:05:59.900
Do?

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:00.900
We're going to sit down.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:01.900
We're going to talk about this calmly.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.900
We're going to talk about it rationally.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:04.900
Oh, isn't this just like you?

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.900
Everything is going to pieces, and you want to be calm and rational.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.900
It doesn't help to get hysterical.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:10.900
Well, then what does?

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.900
If you're such a model father, go ahead.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:14.900
You handle it.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:15.900
Kim, come on.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.900
Let's sit down.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:22.900
Maybe you and I could bridge the generation gap for a moment, huh?

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:23.900
I don't know.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.900
Would you like to try?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:26.900
Okay.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:27.900
Okay.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.900
One question.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.900
Why?

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:32.900
Why did you do it?

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.900
At least you could have asked me if I did do it.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.900
I didn't expect the cops to believe me, but you.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:40.900
All right.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:41.900
Did you do it?

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:42.900
No.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:49.900
The police report said that the car wreaked of marijuana.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.900
Well, it was a Turkish cigarette.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.900
Well, look.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:07:01.900
Look, I've got the rest of the pack right here.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:02.900
She didn't do anything.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:06.900
It was all a mistake.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:07.900
May I go to bed now?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:08.900
Oh, yes, of course.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:09.900
Not yet.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.900
Oh, now, Ted, she's been through enough.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:12.900
Come on, dear.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:13.900
We've both got to stay here.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:14.900
Have a good night's sleep.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:15.900
Forget all about this.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.900
I don't need to be tucked in.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:25.900
Okay.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:28.900
Well, I think we've all had enough for one night.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:29.900
It's late.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:36.900
Carolyn, why didn't you tell me Kim is on probation?

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.900
She made a mistake.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.900
I didn't want to have to make a family dinner conversation.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.900
There is such a thing as family help.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.900
We thought that was the best way to handle it.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.900
I really have had it for one day.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.900
Look, it's late.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.900
Why don't you stay over?

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:57.900
Thanks.

00:07:57.900 --> 00:07:59.900
I'd rather go home.

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:00.900
All right.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:02.900
Good night, dear.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:03.900
Good night.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:15.900
I'll be up in a moment.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.900
Can you do anything?

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:29.900
I'll try.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:30.900
Morning.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:31.900
Good morning.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.900
Coffee?

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:40.900
I wasn't aware you were this anxious to get started on the commissioner's project.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.900
Can you get along without me for a few days?

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.900
There's something I have to take care of.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.900
Sounds serious.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.900
It is.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.900
Yes, we can get along without you for a few days.

00:08:55.900 --> 00:09:03.900
Thank you.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:08.900
Chief.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.900
Do you ever get the feeling that we lose touch sometimes?

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:19.900
All we do is work on cases, but we don't see the people or feel them, even those close to us?

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:25.900
When someone makes a speech like that, it's what they don't say that interests me.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.900
Kim was arrested last night.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:28.900
Kim Channing?

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:29.900
Yes.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:30.900
What's the charge?

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.900
23-105-VC-Drugs.

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:39.900
11-9-10-H&amp;S and 11-5-30-H&amp;S.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:42.900
The arrest report said that the car reeked of marijuana.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:44.900
What does Kim say?

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:48.900
Turkish cigarettes.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.900
Chief, I want to believe her.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.900
She's not just another kid.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.900
I fed her, changed her, held her on my lap.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.900
I watched her grow up.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.900
I feel like her aunt.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:08.900
But when I talk to her, I act more like a cop.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:11.900
What can I do?

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:26.900
What can I help her?

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:27.900
Chief Ironside.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.900
John, how have you been?

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:30.900
Good to see you.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.900
Eve, you bringing in the heavy artillery?

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:33.900
I brought myself in.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.900
Well, I know you like it straight.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:41.900
Kim Channing got the brass ring, her second offense in less than a year.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:49.900
Chances are the youth authority will send her to a girls' school.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.900
What can we do to help her?

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.900
Her only chance is to tell us where she got those drugs,

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:56.900
but I don't think that information will come from her.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.900
Suppose it comes from me.

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:03.900
Then I'll do what I can.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:04.900
Hi, Mr. Ironside.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:06.900
Good morning, Kimberly.

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:07.900
I am.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.900
Carolyn said you remember Chief Ironside.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.900
Yes, of course, Chief.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.900
Sit down, please.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:18.900
Thank you.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.900
Do you both understand the charges?

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:22.900
Yes, sir, we do.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:25.900
Kim, you were informed of your rights last night.

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:26.900
Do you understand them?

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:27.900
Yes.

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.900
Well, tell him about the Turkish cigarettes.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:31.900
Yes, that's all in the arrest report,

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.900
but for your information, Mrs. Channing,

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:41.900
the odor given off by Turkish cigarettes in no way resembles marijuana.

00:11:41.900 --> 00:11:43.900
The main problem is that Kim violated probation

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:48.900
and committed a felony while in your custody.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.900
I'm sorry.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:54.900
You'd think having been through this before, it'd be easier this time.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.900
Please try and believe us.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:57.900
We've tried our best.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:58.900
Her grades were good.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:11:59.900
She never missed class.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:02.900
None of the warning signs you told us about.

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.900
Everything seemed all right.

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:08.900
What were we supposed to do, lock her in her room at night and never let her out?

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:15.900
Sergeant, you tell us what to do.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:21.900
The probation department has decided to remove that responsibility from you.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:24.900
They feel it's in Kim's best interest to hold her until she goes to court.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:25.900
Hold her?

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:26.900
You mean jail?

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:29.900
No, you can't.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.900
In the opinion of the probation department,

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.900
Kim lacks proper parental supervision,

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:38.900
and to leave her in the home would further the chances of her committing additional crimes.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:39.900
Oh, no!

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.900
Let me understand you, Sergeant.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:45.900
Are you saying that we are not fit to raise our own child?

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:46.900
I'm sorry, Mrs. Channing.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:48.900
Don't let them, Ted.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.900
I think it's better if you two wait it outside.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:51.900
But I can't!

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:52.900
It's our baby!

00:12:52.900 --> 00:13:15.900
I'm sorry, Mrs. Channing.

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:22.900
John, how about releasing Kim into my custody, or into Eve's custody?

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.900
Well, Eve is her aunt.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:26.900
Are you willing to take the responsibility?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:30.900
Of course I am.

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:31.900
Maybe that's better.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:34.900
Thank you, John.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:35.900
Thank you.

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:40.900
Now, Kim, you understand what's going on, where you stand?

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:41.900
Yes.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.900
Then it boils down to this.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:47.900
If you tell Sergeant Darga where you got the drugs,

00:13:47.900 --> 00:13:49.900
there's a chance we can help you.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:52.900
I didn't get any drugs.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:53.900
I don't know where they came from.

00:13:53.900 --> 00:13:54.900
If I knew, I'd tell you.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.900
Have a little respect for our intelligence.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.900
You were smoking pot in the car before you were stopped.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.900
Now let's go from there.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.900
Two minutes ago, you were my aunt.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:04.900
Now you're a cop.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:09.900
Kim, if you don't tell us where you got the drugs,

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:15.900
there's nothing we can do to keep you out of that girls' school.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.900
But that's not fair.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:19.900
I didn't steal anything.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:20.900
I didn't hurt anybody.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.900
You broke the law.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:25.900
Laws are made for the protection of everyone,

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.900
even the people who break them.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.900
You sound just like my mom and my dad.

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:32.900
Don't do that.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:34.900
It's bad just because they say so.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:37.900
What makes the law right and me wrong?

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:39.900
We're not talking about the validity of the law.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.900
It's there. It exists.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.900
We're talking about where you got the stuff.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.900
School? At the party?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.900
I don't know.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:52.900
All right, you and Kim go ahead.

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:54.900
Tell Carol and Ted what we've decided.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.900
I want to talk to John for a minute.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.900
Wait for me in the hall.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.900
You really think you can help her?

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:07.900
Maybe it's the kids who weren't arrested last night who need the help.

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:59.900
What brought on the sudden interest in drugs in schools?

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.900
It's personal matters.

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:04.900
You and your personal matters. Why come to me?

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.900
You're on all the committees in this town.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:09.900
If anyone knows what's going on, it would be you.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.900
All my information is second or third hand.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:14.900
Now that I have your permission, I'll get it for you first hand.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:15.900
I haven't got my permission.

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:16.900
Bob, I want a full report.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:18.900
Don't I always give you a full report?

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:21.900
No. And where are those arson statistics?

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:24.900
Mark, I'll have them finished by Monday.

00:16:24.900 --> 00:16:26.900
Next stop, Board of Education.

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:36.900
Chief, if it's all right with you, I'd like to show Kim something.

00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:40.900
Something she'll care about right now?

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:55.900
What's ahead of her if she doesn't straighten up right now?

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:21.900
Control. Right.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:41.900
