It's to a degree.

00:33:51.900 --> 00:33:52.900
I'm a consultant.

00:33:52.900 --> 00:33:57.900
This is Mark Sanger, my interpreter.

00:33:57.900 --> 00:34:00.900
What does a consultant do?

00:34:00.900 --> 00:34:03.900
Give advice.

00:34:03.900 --> 00:34:06.900
I didn't know my mother was a consultant.

00:34:06.900 --> 00:34:12.900
Well, I know mine is, and I would like to get this over with before she comes home.

00:34:12.900 --> 00:34:15.900
I wouldn't want her to think we all got busted.

00:34:15.900 --> 00:34:17.900
Kim Channing disappeared last night.

00:34:17.900 --> 00:34:19.900
We're trying to find her.

00:34:19.900 --> 00:34:21.900
I haven't seen her since...

00:34:21.900 --> 00:34:22.900
Since when?

00:34:22.900 --> 00:34:24.900
Since the day before yesterday at school.

00:34:24.900 --> 00:34:27.900
Were you going to say since you were at a party together?

00:34:27.900 --> 00:34:30.900
Since the day before yesterday at school.

00:34:30.900 --> 00:34:36.900
Oh, I haven't seen her since I had my hepatitis thing.

00:34:36.900 --> 00:34:42.900
Mr. Ironside, we would like to help you, but we don't know where Kim is.

00:34:42.900 --> 00:34:44.900
If you did, would you tell me?

00:34:44.900 --> 00:34:45.900
Of course.

00:34:45.900 --> 00:34:46.900
Not.

00:34:46.900 --> 00:34:48.900
Which is it?

00:34:48.900 --> 00:34:49.900
Both.

00:34:49.900 --> 00:34:51.900
Chris is goody-goody at heart.

00:34:51.900 --> 00:34:52.900
She'd tell.

00:34:52.900 --> 00:34:53.900
But you wouldn't.

00:34:53.900 --> 00:34:56.900
We're up to you, sir, and you're, uh...

00:34:56.900 --> 00:35:04.900
I'm Kim's friend and want to do what's best for her routine.

00:35:04.900 --> 00:35:06.900
Look, can we level?

00:35:06.900 --> 00:35:16.900
Talk to each other honestly, no covering, strictly off the record?

00:35:16.900 --> 00:35:17.900
Why not?

00:35:17.900 --> 00:35:19.900
As long as we understand one thing.

00:35:19.900 --> 00:35:23.900
You're the enemy, and we all know it.

00:35:23.900 --> 00:35:27.900
You all turn on, don't you?

00:35:27.900 --> 00:35:29.900
Once in a while.

00:35:29.900 --> 00:35:32.900
I don't.

00:35:32.900 --> 00:35:36.900
I refuse to answer on whatever grounds people refuse to answer on.

00:35:36.900 --> 00:35:37.900
Tell me why.

00:35:37.900 --> 00:35:39.900
It's groovy.

00:35:39.900 --> 00:35:41.900
Makes the whole lousy world a little better.

00:35:41.900 --> 00:35:44.900
How groovy is it when you get strung out?

00:35:44.900 --> 00:35:46.900
You just drop its opposite and get even.

00:35:46.900 --> 00:35:48.900
Even's a nice high, right in the middle.

00:35:48.900 --> 00:35:54.900
Not too far up and not too far down.

00:35:54.900 --> 00:35:57.900
Has anyone ever told you about barbiturate convulsions?

00:35:57.900 --> 00:35:59.900
That's for someone who's hooked.

00:35:59.900 --> 00:36:00.900
We're not.

00:36:00.900 --> 00:36:01.900
We can put down any time we want.

00:36:01.900 --> 00:36:04.900
I've heard that from a lot of addicts.

00:36:04.900 --> 00:36:06.900
The time to stop is before you start.

00:36:06.900 --> 00:36:08.900
Under the law...

00:36:08.900 --> 00:36:12.900
I thought you wanted to level, and you're pulling the law in on us.

00:36:12.900 --> 00:36:13.900
The law meant to protect you.

00:36:13.900 --> 00:36:19.900
Look, Mr. Ironside, pretty soon we're going to have to go out into that society of yours and do our thing.

00:36:19.900 --> 00:36:21.900
And be nice, respectable people like our parents.

00:36:21.900 --> 00:36:22.900
And you.

00:36:22.900 --> 00:36:23.900
And we know it.

00:36:23.900 --> 00:36:25.900
And when that time comes, we'll put it down.

00:36:25.900 --> 00:36:27.900
You're part of that society now.

00:36:27.900 --> 00:36:28.900
You have your thing.

00:36:28.900 --> 00:36:29.900
You're responsible.

00:36:29.900 --> 00:36:31.900
Then why don't you treat us like that?

00:36:31.900 --> 00:36:32.900
You know, we hurt, too.

00:36:32.900 --> 00:36:34.900
I don't mean aches and pains.

00:36:34.900 --> 00:36:36.900
I mean hurt, deep inside.

00:36:36.900 --> 00:36:38.900
Just like everybody else in the world.

00:36:38.900 --> 00:36:40.900
Does that include older people?

00:36:40.900 --> 00:36:41.900
Sure.

00:36:41.900 --> 00:36:42.900
They hurt, too.

00:36:42.900 --> 00:36:44.900
But they have crutches.

00:36:44.900 --> 00:36:45.900
Booze.

00:36:45.900 --> 00:36:46.900
Gambling.

00:36:46.900 --> 00:36:47.900
Sex.

00:36:47.900 --> 00:36:49.900
And what do we have?

00:36:49.900 --> 00:36:50.900
Except grass.

00:36:50.900 --> 00:36:52.900
And it takes the pain away.

00:36:52.900 --> 00:36:56.900
Christine, your friends play around with drugs, and you don't.

00:36:56.900 --> 00:37:02.900
I'll drop an upper once in a while to get through a test, but I wouldn't call that taking drugs.

00:37:02.900 --> 00:37:03.900
What do you call it?

00:37:03.900 --> 00:37:07.900
Better education through chemistry.

00:37:07.900 --> 00:37:11.900
I don't suppose you've ever turned anybody in who was dealing to your friends.

00:37:11.900 --> 00:37:12.900
No.

00:37:12.900 --> 00:37:16.900
If they want to buy that stuff, it's their business, not mine.

00:37:16.900 --> 00:37:20.900
Would you call the police if you saw a burglar climbing in one of your neighbor's windows?

00:37:20.900 --> 00:37:23.900
That's a poor analogy, Mr. Ironside.

00:37:23.900 --> 00:37:26.900
Really?

00:37:26.900 --> 00:37:30.900
Next time you see a burglar, think about it.

00:37:30.900 --> 00:37:33.900
Well, thank you, girls.

00:37:33.900 --> 00:37:36.900
You're all alone on frozen ground.

00:37:36.900 --> 00:37:39.900
Your friends go on without you.

00:37:39.900 --> 00:37:45.900
And now that devil's on the phone, you've got no place to run to.

00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:52.900
You walked across a river bridge one day when you were smiling.

00:37:52.900 --> 00:37:55.900
Well, Mark, I'm glad you're here.

00:37:55.900 --> 00:38:00.900
You were smiling.

00:38:00.900 --> 00:38:06.900
Well, Mark, two of them are halfway there, and Susan has already made it.

00:38:16.900 --> 00:38:18.900
Have you the details on her first arrest?

00:38:18.900 --> 00:38:20.900
Yeah, it was ten months ago.

00:38:20.900 --> 00:38:22.900
She was one of seven arrested at a party.

00:38:22.900 --> 00:38:26.900
I called the police because they saw kids running around the house naked.

00:38:26.900 --> 00:38:28.900
How about the names of the others arrested at the party?

00:38:28.900 --> 00:38:30.900
Got them right here. You want me to bring them up?

00:38:30.900 --> 00:38:32.900
Yeah, please.

00:38:32.900 --> 00:38:34.900
How will that help?

00:38:34.900 --> 00:38:38.900
We have to look for other friends or connections.

00:38:38.900 --> 00:38:41.900
She's become dependent on drugs.

00:38:41.900 --> 00:38:44.900
She won't be very far away from her source of supply.

00:38:44.900 --> 00:38:46.900
I don't think she's hooked.

00:38:46.900 --> 00:38:48.900
She said she took them now and then just for kicks.

00:38:48.900 --> 00:38:51.900
Eve, I seem to have heard that before.

00:38:51.900 --> 00:38:57.900
I knew guys strung out so far they were twinging, and they still swore they could put on.

00:38:57.900 --> 00:39:02.900
Here's a school personnel breakdown at the time of her first arrest.

00:39:02.900 --> 00:39:04.900
And read those.

00:39:04.900 --> 00:39:05.900
What is it?

00:39:05.900 --> 00:39:07.900
Underground papers.

00:39:07.900 --> 00:39:09.900
Each of them has an article on marijuana.

00:39:09.900 --> 00:39:14.900
I don't know where to buy it.

00:39:14.900 --> 00:39:17.900
I tell good stuff from bad.

00:39:17.900 --> 00:39:22.900
How to roll it, how to smoke it.

00:39:22.900 --> 00:39:24.900
How to spot a narcotics officer.

00:39:24.900 --> 00:39:26.900
What to do if you spot one.

00:39:26.900 --> 00:39:36.900
Well, maybe we ought to be on their subscription list.

00:39:36.900 --> 00:39:38.900
You look terrible. Did you ever get any sleep?

00:39:38.900 --> 00:39:41.900
With my kind of a caseload, 14 last night.

00:39:41.900 --> 00:39:43.900
So far this year it's doubled.

00:39:43.900 --> 00:39:45.900
What are we doing about these?

00:39:45.900 --> 00:39:51.900
If we can prove that two or three of these kids started using pot as a direct result of one of these articles, we can nail the author for contributing.

00:39:51.900 --> 00:39:52.900
And that's all?

00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:55.900
It's not as much of a headache as these spontaneous demonstrations.

00:39:55.900 --> 00:39:59.900
With the printed instructions and the signs where the kids can get grass and pills free.

00:39:59.900 --> 00:40:01.900
Oh, that's the list you wanted.

00:40:01.900 --> 00:40:07.900
Any additional beefs against any of them since the party are underlined.

00:40:07.900 --> 00:40:10.900
Why was the sales charge against that Terry Lawrence dropped?

00:40:10.900 --> 00:40:15.900
Defense of entrapment, insufficient evidence.

00:40:15.900 --> 00:40:44.900
Possible sales, possible source of supply.

00:40:44.900 --> 00:40:56.900
Terry Lawrence.

00:40:56.900 --> 00:40:57.900
Yes.

00:40:57.900 --> 00:40:58.900
Police.

00:40:58.900 --> 00:41:01.900
I can ask you a few questions about Kimberly Channing.

00:41:01.900 --> 00:41:11.900
Oh, come on in.

00:41:11.900 --> 00:41:15.900
Kim Channing disappeared last night.

00:41:15.900 --> 00:41:19.900
We'd like any information you might have that can help us locate her.

00:41:19.900 --> 00:41:22.900
Well, I don't have any.

00:41:22.900 --> 00:41:24.900
What do you run?

00:41:24.900 --> 00:41:27.900
Oh, 1500 meters, but I don't run anymore.

00:41:27.900 --> 00:41:29.900
Why not?

00:41:29.900 --> 00:41:31.900
Say, do you mind if I ask you a question?

00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:32.900
Certainly.

00:41:32.900 --> 00:41:35.900
Why ask me about Kim Channing?

00:41:35.900 --> 00:41:38.900
We're questioning everyone who was arrested with her at the party.

00:41:38.900 --> 00:41:43.900
Oh, sure. Well, that stuff I took at the party is the reason I don't run anymore.

00:41:43.900 --> 00:41:48.900
But, uh, well, I got hip and I put down.

00:41:48.900 --> 00:41:51.900
That's smart of you.

00:41:51.900 --> 00:41:57.900
Look, I wish I could help you find Kim, but I haven't seen her since the party.

00:41:57.900 --> 00:41:59.900
You haven't seen her since the party?

00:41:59.900 --> 00:42:00.900
Yeah, that's right.

00:42:00.900 --> 00:42:06.900
Mind if we look around?

00:42:06.900 --> 00:42:08.900
Yes, as a matter of fact, I do.

00:42:08.900 --> 00:42:12.900
I can have a search warrant here within five minutes.

00:42:12.900 --> 00:42:17.900
Don't hassle him.

00:42:17.900 --> 00:42:19.900
I came here on my own free will.

00:42:19.900 --> 00:42:22.900
Kim.

00:42:22.900 --> 00:42:29.900
Get dressed.

00:42:29.900 --> 00:42:43.900
Still mind if we look around?

00:42:43.900 --> 00:42:50.900
Don't look at me like I killed somebody.

00:42:50.900 --> 00:42:52.900
Aren't you just a little ashamed?

00:42:52.900 --> 00:42:55.900
No, I'm not.

00:42:55.900 --> 00:42:57.900
I think you mean it.

00:42:57.900 --> 00:43:00.900
I do.

00:43:00.900 --> 00:43:03.900
I came here because Terry was the only one I could turn to.

00:43:03.900 --> 00:43:05.900
He understands me and trusts me.

00:43:05.900 --> 00:43:21.900
I can trust him any time, any place, anywhere.

00:43:21.900 --> 00:43:24.900
I said search the apartment, not play around with his food.

00:43:24.900 --> 00:43:27.900
A lot of cats hide their weed in the bottom of cereal boxes.

00:43:27.900 --> 00:43:31.900
Another magazine article.

00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:35.900
Well, what do you know?

00:43:35.900 --> 00:43:44.900
The magazine was wrecked.

00:43:44.900 --> 00:43:46.900
You ready to tell us about it?

00:43:46.900 --> 00:43:48.900
Man, most of the time I just sold the stuff for what it cost me.

00:43:48.900 --> 00:43:50.900
I didn't make a dime.

00:43:50.900 --> 00:43:51.900
That's not very good business.

00:43:51.900 --> 00:43:53.900
I wasn't in business.

00:43:53.900 --> 00:43:58.900
Terry was just one of the stuff and I knew where to get it.

00:43:58.900 --> 00:44:01.900
Right now the charges are possession and contributing.

00:44:01.900 --> 00:44:05.900
But do you realize the gravity of a sales charge?

00:44:05.900 --> 00:44:07.900
I never thought about it.

00:44:07.900 --> 00:44:10.900
Did you get your drugs from Terry?

00:44:10.900 --> 00:44:12.900
No.

00:44:12.900 --> 00:44:15.900
What's so funny?

00:44:15.900 --> 00:44:18.900
Well, that I'm being charged for contributing.

00:44:18.900 --> 00:44:20.900
Why?

00:44:20.900 --> 00:44:24.900
Kim's the one who turned me on.

00:44:24.900 --> 00:44:31.900
Two years ago.

00:44:31.900 --> 00:44:38.900
Oh, my darling.

00:44:38.900 --> 00:44:41.900
We'll come every visiting day, huh?

00:44:41.900 --> 00:44:42.900
Take care of yourself, huh?

00:44:42.900 --> 00:44:45.900
I will.

00:44:45.900 --> 00:44:46.900
Bye, Aunt Eve.

00:44:46.900 --> 00:44:47.900
Bye, Kim.

00:44:47.900 --> 00:44:50.900
The year will be over before you know it.

00:44:50.900 --> 00:44:55.900
Thank you.

00:44:55.900 --> 00:44:57.900
Maybe I should have been a drunk.

00:44:57.900 --> 00:45:00.900
At least alcohol is legal.

00:45:00.900 --> 00:45:02.900
The candy cane slips from your hand.

00:45:02.900 --> 00:45:05.900
Magician draws the curtain.

00:45:05.900 --> 00:45:08.900
The crutch you held to help you stand

00:45:08.900 --> 00:45:11.900
Has made you feel uncertain.

00:45:11.900 --> 00:45:14.900
You walked across a river bridge.

00:45:14.900 --> 00:45:17.900
One day when you were smiling.

00:45:17.900 --> 00:45:20.900
Now the sun has turned to brick.

00:45:20.900 --> 00:45:24.900
The road you're on is winding.

00:45:24.900 --> 00:45:30.900
You lost your way the other day.

00:45:30.900 --> 00:45:34.900
Seeking the melody now.

00:45:34.900 --> 00:45:38.900
Well, include these totals, Eve.

00:45:38.900 --> 00:45:42.900
They cover the area from the Presidio to the Embarcadero.

00:45:42.900 --> 00:45:44.900
Eve.

00:45:44.900 --> 00:45:46.900
Oh, I'm sorry, Jim.

00:45:46.900 --> 00:45:48.900
Arson statistics don't mean very much

00:45:48.900 --> 00:45:53.900
When you've just had a fire in your own path.

00:45:53.900 --> 00:45:56.900
The fire isn't even out.

00:45:56.900 --> 00:46:00.900
Thirty percent of all the high school students are turning on.

00:46:00.900 --> 00:46:03.900
Do we lock them all up?

00:46:03.900 --> 00:46:05.900
Lack of communication.

00:46:05.900 --> 00:46:08.900
The whole thing reminds me of the War of 1812.

00:46:08.900 --> 00:46:11.900
It was settled by a great treaty.

00:46:11.900 --> 00:46:13.900
I got a D in history.

00:46:13.900 --> 00:46:15.900
The Battle of New Orleans

00:46:15.900 --> 00:46:18.900
Was the bloodiest battle of that war.

00:46:18.900 --> 00:46:20.900
Because of a lack of communication,

00:46:20.900 --> 00:46:25.900
It was fought 15 days after the treaty had been signed.

00:46:25.900 --> 00:46:27.900
Someone to see you, Chief.

00:46:27.900 --> 00:46:31.900
Well, Christine, what brings you into the enemy camp?

00:46:31.900 --> 00:46:33.900
Well, I...

00:46:33.900 --> 00:46:39.900
I saw a burglar last night.

00:46:39.900 --> 00:46:43.900
My sister, in junior high, she's only 13.

00:46:43.900 --> 00:46:46.900
Well, a boy in her class showed up with a handful of pills,

00:46:46.900 --> 00:46:54.900
And he's only 13, too.

00:46:54.900 --> 00:46:59.900
That's his name.

00:46:59.900 --> 00:47:04.900
Thank you.

00:47:04.900 --> 00:47:10.900
I guess now I'm a fink.

00:47:10.900 --> 00:47:15.900
I think you've been a friend, Christine.

00:47:15.900 --> 00:47:17.900
More than a friend.

00:47:17.900 --> 00:47:23.900
Not only to your sister, but to a lot of people you don't even know.

00:47:23.900 --> 00:47:33.900
Well, I... I hope...

00:47:33.900 --> 00:47:34.900
What was that all about?

00:47:34.900 --> 00:47:38.900
Communication.

00:47:38.900 --> 00:48:05.900
Maybe there won't have to be a Battle of New Orleans.

00:48:08.900 --> 00:48:13.900
